  "slug": "disorder-chern-plateaus-7d05",
  "summary": "Six November 2026 preprints treat disorder, defects and scattering as determinants of Chern plateaus, orbital Hall and magnetoelectric responses, and magnetotransport.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is that disorder and defects are treated as determinants of transport rather than perturbations, though the items differ in scope. In twisted bilayer MoTe2, layer-dependent disorder shapes integer and fractional Chern plateau widths and transitions. Orbital-response studies extend this: Kubo-Bastin Chebyshev calculations address disorder robustness and tunability of the quadrupole-origin orbital Hall effect in a centrosymmetric sp3 lattice; point defects enhance and activate orbital magnetoelectric responses in an orbital antiferromagnet; and structural and electrostatic disorder, including amorphous graphene, yields orbital Hall currents absent in pristine systems. The multi-Weyl work instead goes beyond constant relaxation time, including orbital moment and intervalley scattering. The orbital exchange study in MoS2 concerns clean-limit Hall responses without spin or spin-orbit coupling.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
